{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_51","type":"agent_message","text":"Validated the new focused experiment and its admission prerequisite. Submitting it now; the controller will compile and run `decided_stopsign_only_decide_is_resent`, and the resulting receipt will tell us whether the resend path clamps (stall) or repairs.\n\n{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Added a minimal, directly constructed witness for the active StopSign-resync question and submitted it for execution. The new test `decided_stopsign_only_decide_is_resent` builds five nodes with a 1000-tick election timeout so leadership cannot change, decides entries 1..2 everywhere, then reconfigures while discarding both the AcceptStopSign addressed to node 5 and the leader's first Decide to it. `ready` records the admission premise (node 5 accepted/decided 2 and promised to the leader) before the loss; `after_resend` records, after 150 ticks with all messages delivered, node 5's accepted/decided/leader/promise state, the leader's decided index, `decision_gap`, the number of Decide/Prepare/AcceptSync/AcceptStopSign messages the leader sent to node 5, and the last Decide sequence counter. The declared comparison asserts `decision_gap == 0` for any admitted run in which at least one Decide reached node 5, so a clamped resend produces a violated but complete comparison; a sequence-break recovery would show up as Prepare/AcceptSync traffic and a closed gap. Two supporting sources were registered: the sequence-number status check (util.rs) and the follower's sequence handling (follower.rs).\"}"}}
